---
import FeatureCard from '@chassis-ui/docs/components/FeatureCard.astro'
---

<section class="home-section py-3xl md:py-6xl">
  <div class="container 2xl section-content">
    <div class="grid mb-3xl md:mb-6xl">
      <header class="section-header col-span-full lg:col-span-10 lg:col-start-2 xl:col-span-8 xl:col-start-3 text-center">
        <h2 class="section-title font-3xl md:font-4xl lg:font-5xl mb-xs md:mb-sm lg:mb-md">
          <span class="font-normal d-block">A repository of icons</span> for each team
        </h2>
        <p class="section-body md:font-lg lg:font-xl m-0">
          A team keeps its icons in a repository of its own, with <code>@chassis-ui/icons</code> as
          a development dependency. The builder ships no icons: everything that is particular to a
          set is in its repository.
        </p>
      </header>
    </div>

    <div class="section-features grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-md md:gap-xl">
      <div>
        <FeatureCard icon="cx-folders">
          <Fragment slot="title">One file per icon</Fragment>
          <Fragment slot="body">
            Save <code>&lt;name&gt;.svg</code> into <code>source/</code>, and the icon is in the
            next build. The name of the file is the name of the icon, and no list of icons is kept
            beside the files.
          </Fragment>
        </FeatureCard>
      </div>
      <div>
        <FeatureCard icon="cx-swatchbook">
          <Fragment slot="title">Settings in package.json</Fragment>
          <Fragment slot="body">
            The <code>chassis.build</code> block names the font and the class prefix, and sets the
            frame, the styles, the font formats and the targets. <code>init</code> writes it for
            your font name.
          </Fragment>
        </FeatureCard>
      </div>
      <div>
        <FeatureCard icon="cx-bullseye-arrow">
          <Fragment slot="title">Code points that stay</Fragment>
          <Fragment slot="body">
            An icon keeps its code point in the font for as long as it is in the set. The build
            records them in <code>codepoints.json</code>, and gives the code point of a removed icon
            to no later icon.
          </Fragment>
        </FeatureCard>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
